{"availability":"available","full":"AhadAhmad0/fraud-detection-llm-explainer","name":"fraud-detection-llm-explainer","description":"Credit card fraud detection with XGBoost. SHAP shows why a transaction was flagged and an LLM explains it in plain English. Live Streamlit demo.","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-14T13:05:47Z","updated":"2026-10-06T17:04:08Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://fraud-detection-llm-explainer.streamlit.app/","topics":["explainable-ai","fraud-detection","imbalanced-data","llm","machine-learning","python","shap","smote","streamlit","xgboost"],"demo":"https://fraud-detection-llm-explainer.streamlit.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T02:59:21.366Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T02:59:21.366Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T02:59:21.366Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T18:25:29.046Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-11T06:12:32.710Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-17T02:59:21.366Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A fraud detection system in two parts. An XGBoost classifier flags suspicious transactions. SHAP finds the features behind each flag, and an LLM turns that into a short plain-English explanation for a human reviewer.","A lot of GenAI projects are a chat API with a UI on top. I wanted one built around a real constraint. In fraud and risk work, a model can flag a transaction, but a person still has to decide whether to trust the flag.","So the LLM here makes no decisions. The classifier detects, SHAP attributes, and the LLM only rewrites SHAP's output as text. I kept it this way on purpose. A fraud decision should come from a model that can be audited, and the LLM should only help a person understand that decision."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AhadAhmad0/fraud-detection-llm-explainer/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"ce15ebb8021056716b2b660e6258090123d5f508c229d3